\subtree{
  \title{Decision}
  \p{Each decision has a stable ID, decision/rationale/rejected text, tests, status, affected declarations, and supersession links. Revision 1 gives changed historical decisions new IDs; \code{12-revision-notes.md} is the crosswalk and \code{history/v0/} contains the exact old text. Current references resolve to current IDs; references to history are explicitly marked historical. Future changes to a frozen decision also receive a new ID. A human-authorized design revision may supersede frozen choices; permission is not requested again for the already authorized revision.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rationale}
  \p{Preserve why choices changed without letting old claims govern new proofs.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Rejected}
  \p{Reusing a frozen ID for a changed mathematical statement or deleting its rationale.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Acceptance}
  \p{Revision crosswalk validation and \ref{ms-0000}/\ref{ms-foundation} registry audit.}
}
\subtree{
  \title{Status}
  \p{frozen policy; current provisional choices remain amendable by recorded decisions.}
}
